# Run artefacts. Every script writes its server log, unix socket, response
# headers and advisory-lock FIFO NEXT TO ITSELF, so a run dirties this directory.
# None of it is source, and a socket cannot be committed at all.
#
# Deliberately NOT a blanket `*` with exceptions: a new script must be added
# explicitly, so it cannot be silently ignored the way an untracked harness was
# the whole problem this directory exists to fix.
*.log
*.sock.*
.lock.*
.plock.*
.elock.*
.wlock.*
h.*
ph.*
eh.*
wh.*
dh.*
# A local DSN file. The harness reads its credentials from the environment; if
# you keep one here for convenience it must never be committed.
dsn
